  "ref": "DEU.6.20",
  "review_notes": [
    "*mean* (t012) moved out of the מָה unit and marked `added`. Rule 20 states that the construction supplies the copula and nothing more, and that a whole lexical verb supplied for a verbless Hebrew clause is `added`; its test — ask which morpheme is there to carry the English — finds only an interrogative pronoun, whose rendering *What* is already complete, and a clause with no verb in it licenses no verb.",
    "The competing reading, taken by the previous alignment, treats *mean* as the English realization of the predicative interrogative on the analogy of מִי הָאִישׁ הַלָּזֶה → *What man is this*; that analogy supports a copula, not a lexical predicate.",
    "*in time to come* left whole with מָחָר and headed on *time*; heading on *come* remains available under rule 31."
  ]
}
